WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience applauding)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.123
- All right, it's good to see you again.

00:00:02.123 --> 00:00:03.267
- Always good to be back.
- Meet everybody.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:04.107
- I got to meet everybody, which is good.

00:00:04.107 --> 00:00:04.940
- Hello.
- All right.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:05.773
You go way back.

00:00:05.773 --> 00:00:06.606
- We do.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:07.949
- We bring people together
on the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:00:07.949 --> 00:00:10.237
So your latest book though,
is about John Lewis.

00:00:10.237 --> 00:00:11.070
This is incredible.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.635
So you worked with him, right, to do this?

00:00:12.635 --> 00:00:14.357
- Yeah, so John Lewis is
one of the first people

00:00:14.357 --> 00:00:16.288
who worked with us on other books.

00:00:16.288 --> 00:00:17.976
He loved our Rosa Parks book.

00:00:17.976 --> 00:00:18.809
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah.

00:00:18.809 --> 00:00:20.405
- And when we did our I am
Martin Luther King Jr. book,

00:00:20.405 --> 00:00:22.888
I was like, well, I
can go and ask for help

00:00:22.888 --> 00:00:25.848
but why don't I ask the
guy who was with Dr. King?

00:00:25.848 --> 00:00:28.708
And so he was our advisor on
I am Martin Luther King Jr.

00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:29.541
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh, wow.

00:00:29.541 --> 00:00:30.374
(audience cheering)

00:00:30.374 --> 00:00:31.207
- So, which was amazing.

00:00:31.207 --> 00:00:32.229
And when we did the I Am John Lewis book,

00:00:32.229 --> 00:00:33.856
obviously, he had passed away-

00:00:33.856 --> 00:00:34.689
- Yeah.

00:00:34.689 --> 00:00:36.385
- But his lessons are just as vital today.

00:00:36.385 --> 00:00:37.218
- Yeah.

00:00:37.218 --> 00:00:38.395
- And, you know, it starts with that idea,

00:00:38.395 --> 00:00:40.567
what do you do when you
see something unfair?

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:41.506
Do you get mad?

00:00:41.506 --> 00:00:42.346
Do you cry?

00:00:42.346 --> 00:00:44.494
Do you storm off or do you march forward

00:00:44.494 --> 00:00:46.328
and try to do something about it?

00:00:46.328 --> 00:00:48.154
And that's what the
book really tries to do

00:00:48.154 --> 00:00:50.128
because he always tried
to do something about it.

00:00:50.128 --> 00:00:51.477
He used nonviolence resistance

00:00:51.477 --> 00:00:54.985
and he would always make
sure to fight back against,

00:00:54.985 --> 00:00:57.776
you know, make sure
whether it was the sit-ins,

00:00:57.776 --> 00:00:59.922
whether it was obviously the marches,

00:00:59.922 --> 00:01:01.620
he would never lose his temper,

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.276
would train himself to
never lose his temper.

00:01:04.276 --> 00:01:07.664
- So, your books always start
with the person as a kid,

00:01:07.664 --> 00:01:08.784
so what did you learn?

00:01:08.784 --> 00:01:10.664
- Yeah, so this one, it's amazing.

00:01:10.664 --> 00:01:13.260
You know, his parents
told him, "You know what,

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.968
just don't get in trouble.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:16.032
Just lay low."

00:01:16.032 --> 00:01:18.224
But his grandmother was built differently.

00:01:18.224 --> 00:01:19.836
And his grandmother, if
you were black back then

00:01:19.836 --> 00:01:20.728
when he was growing up,

00:01:20.728 --> 00:01:22.860
and someone was white
coming down the street,

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.544
you were expected that you'd
have to walk out of the way.

00:01:25.544 --> 00:01:27.628
You literally had to make
way for that white person.

00:01:27.628 --> 00:01:29.304
And his grandmother was like,

00:01:29.304 --> 00:01:31.399
"That's an unfair rule,
I'm not doing that."

00:01:31.399 --> 00:01:32.232
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah.

00:01:32.232 --> 00:01:33.065
- And she'll respectfully just be,

00:01:33.065 --> 00:01:36.116
"You have a good day now," but
stay exactly where she was.

00:01:36.116 --> 00:01:36.949
- Wow.

00:01:36.949 --> 00:01:38.812
- And he knew from her, from Dr. King,

00:01:38.812 --> 00:01:41.348
from the lessons of Rosa Parks that,

00:01:41.348 --> 00:01:43.028
you know what, you have to make sure

00:01:43.028 --> 00:01:45.364
that you get into what
he called good trouble.

00:01:45.364 --> 00:01:47.844
And good trouble is necessary trouble.

00:01:47.844 --> 00:01:49.427
Good trouble is the kind of trouble,

00:01:49.427 --> 00:01:51.440
when you see someone and an injustice,

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.716
like you were talking
about, or something unfair,

00:01:53.716 --> 00:01:55.012
and you're fighting against it.

00:01:55.012 --> 00:01:57.188
That's the kind of good trouble
we all need to get into.

00:01:57.188 --> 00:01:59.660
- Yeah, what a great lesson
that is, good trouble.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:01.012
I've never heard it put like that.

00:02:01.012 --> 00:02:02.332
So, there's a passage in the book

00:02:02.332 --> 00:02:03.908
that speaks to that, right?

00:02:03.908 --> 00:02:05.687
- Yeah, so, and you know,
and one of the things

00:02:05.687 --> 00:02:06.968
that's so important when you think of it,

00:02:06.968 --> 00:02:08.565
and I'm gonna read you from this passage,

00:02:08.565 --> 00:02:12.036
is that they asked him,
how do you stay calm?

00:02:12.036 --> 00:02:14.768
Right? How do you stay calm
when people are yelling at you

00:02:14.768 --> 00:02:16.564
and throwing things at
you and spitting at you?

00:02:16.564 --> 00:02:18.648
And he would say, "I have faith."

00:02:18.648 --> 00:02:21.963
And his idea of faith was
that it's not easy, it's hard.

00:02:21.963 --> 00:02:24.708
But faith to him was, you
believe in something so strongly

00:02:24.708 --> 00:02:26.978
you make a way outta no way.

00:02:26.978 --> 00:02:28.601
And I love that idea, Kelly, right?

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:29.434
- Wow.

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:30.468
- You're making a way outta no way.

00:02:30.468 --> 00:02:31.560
So here's the part I wanted to read

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:32.748
and this is the end of the book.

00:02:32.748 --> 00:02:33.952
It says, "I have faith in my dreams.

00:02:33.952 --> 00:02:35.436
I have faith in this country.

00:02:35.436 --> 00:02:38.468
I have faith that we can
make a way out of no way.

00:02:38.468 --> 00:02:40.652
And in that, I am unshakable.

00:02:40.652 --> 00:02:41.632
We are one people.

00:02:41.632 --> 00:02:42.932
We are one family.

00:02:42.932 --> 00:02:45.368
And now it's time for you to do your part.

00:02:45.368 --> 00:02:48.668
Stand up, speak up, be prepared to march.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.335
It's your turn now.

00:02:51.502 --> 00:02:52.481
I am John Lewis.

00:02:52.481 --> 00:02:56.122
I am never afraid to get in good trouble."

00:02:56.122 --> 00:02:57.278
(audience applauding)

00:02:57.278 --> 00:02:58.111
- Wow.

00:03:00.177 --> 00:03:03.386
It's such a powerful way to educate kids.

00:03:03.386 --> 00:03:06.191
It's really important and
very cool what you do.

00:03:06.191 --> 00:03:07.753
So I just want to thank you
again for doing what you do.

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:08.893
- No, and lessons for my own kids too.

00:03:08.893 --> 00:03:10.225
I know your kids read 'em.
- Yeah.

00:03:10.225 --> 00:03:12.012
- I just am trying to be a good parent.

00:03:12.012 --> 00:03:12.845
- Yeah.

00:03:12.845 --> 00:03:14.060
- We all get so frustrated,

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.137
we all get caught up in the world,

00:03:15.137 --> 00:03:17.357
but this is my soul in book form.

00:03:17.357 --> 00:03:18.825
This is how I get to tell my kids,

00:03:18.825 --> 00:03:20.308
here are the values you need to live by.

00:03:20.308 --> 00:03:22.500
And I want my kids to
know, if you see injustice,

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.790
don't stay quiet.

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:24.623
- Speak up.

00:03:24.623 --> 00:03:25.456
- Speak up.

00:03:25.456 --> 00:03:26.289
Use your voice, right?
- Yeah.

00:03:26.289 --> 00:03:27.122
- Find that faith.

00:03:27.122 --> 00:03:28.910
Make a way out of no way.

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:31.230
- Absolutely. Um,
(giggles) so before we go,

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.270
you still write books for
adults as well, right?

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:34.862
- Yeah, so I entertain your kids

00:03:34.862 --> 00:03:36.300
and I also murder people in thrillers.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:37.133
(audience laughing)

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:38.270
That's perfect segue.

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:39.103
- Nice.

00:03:39.103 --> 00:03:40.605
- But what we do, we have
the new thriller's come out.

00:03:40.605 --> 00:03:41.750
This is actually a nonfiction book.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.124
It's called The Nazi Conspiracy.

00:03:43.124 --> 00:03:43.998
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh.

00:03:43.998 --> 00:03:45.197
- It's about a secret plot, a true story,

00:03:45.197 --> 00:03:48.713
for the Nazis where they
tried to kill FDR and Stalin

00:03:48.713 --> 00:03:51.099
and Winston Churchill at
the height of World War II.

00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:51.981
It is a real story.

00:03:51.981 --> 00:03:53.535
It will blow your mind.

00:03:53.535 --> 00:03:54.738
It's all real, out now.

00:03:54.738 --> 00:03:57.754
And it, you know what, I don't
think it's good for your kids

00:03:57.754 --> 00:03:59.906
but I think you'll really, really like it.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:02.394
And it's a way to entertain
and learn about history.

00:04:02.394 --> 00:04:04.845
- I love that it's non-fiction,
that's the scary part.

00:04:04.845 --> 00:04:06.032
Okay.
(audience laughing)

00:04:06.032 --> 00:04:06.865
- Yeah, I know, right?

00:04:06.865 --> 00:04:07.698
That's where we are.

00:04:07.698 --> 00:04:08.748
Look where we are, right?
- Um, yes, I know.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:09.729
- We're back again, fighting Nazis.

00:04:09.729 --> 00:04:10.562
It's unbelievable.

00:04:10.562 --> 00:04:12.554
- It is. It's unbelievable.

00:04:12.554 --> 00:04:14.484
- And that's why we do John Lewis, right?

00:04:14.484 --> 00:04:15.317
- Yeah.

00:04:15.317 --> 00:04:16.150
- I mean it's always-

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:16.983
- That's why it's
important to educate, yeah.

00:04:16.983 --> 00:04:17.899
- A 100%.
- So we don't repeat.

00:04:17.899 --> 00:04:19.107
- Fight back, don't stay quiet.

00:04:19.107 --> 00:04:20.256
- Yeah.
- Use your voice.

00:04:20.256 --> 00:04:21.157
- Absolutely.

00:04:21.157 --> 00:04:21.990
- Wow.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.241
- Thank you so much.
- Always good to see you.

00:04:23.241 --> 00:04:24.074
(audience applauding)

00:04:24.074 --> 00:04:26.385
- I Am John Lewis by Brad
Meltzer's out next week y'all.

00:04:26.385 --> 00:04:28.067
Be sure to check out Brad's entire series

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.008
of Ordinary People Change the World,

00:04:30.008 --> 00:04:32.923
including my personal
favorite, I Am Dolly Parton.

00:04:32.923 --> 00:04:34.010
Guess what everybody?

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:36.052
Everyone is going home with both copies,

00:04:36.052 --> 00:04:38.535
John Lewis and Dolly Parton.

00:04:38.535 --> 00:04:39.368
That's right.

00:04:39.368 --> 00:04:40.388
(audience applauding and cheering)

